WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.690
- But first, Santa comes
down the chimney in 11 days

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.290
to deliver toys everywhere, people.

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:07.250
So this week we've asked all of you

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:09.150
to nominate some real-life Santas

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:10.600
who make our world a better place

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.970
'cause we need these stories,
we love these stories.

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:15.520
All you had to do was pull
out your Pilot G-2 Gel ink pen

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.430
the go-to pen of the
"Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.310
and write us a letter
about a real life St. Nic.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:24.004
So today's letter comes
from Kelli, great name.

00:00:24.004 --> 00:00:24.837
(audience laughing)

00:00:24.837 --> 00:00:27.530
She's a reporter from also great place,

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:29.470
my home state of Texas.

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:30.970
We have Kelli in our audience.

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:32.820
So can you read us what
you wrote, Kelli, hi.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.070
- Yes, hi Kelly.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:36.570
I spell it with an I not a with Y.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.444
But it's okay, it's still the same name.

00:00:38.444 --> 00:00:39.890
- It's okay, we're still
hanging, we're cool.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:41.830
- Okay, I wrote dear Kelly,

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:46.160
I'd like to nominate Willa
Johnson as a real-life Santa.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.220
Every week she drives 100 miles

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:52.250
from her home in Fort
Worth to Athens, Texas

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:53.630
to deliver home cooked meals,

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:57.940
she makes herself for
kids in low-income areas.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:00:59.010
When Willa was a kid,

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:01.440
her mom dropped her off
at a community center.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.910
One day they served moldy sandwiches.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:07.260
Willa promised, when she grew up,

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:10.780
she would never let a kid eat
something that's not fresh.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.929
It has to be something full
of sugar, butter, and love.

00:01:14.929 --> 00:01:16.700
(audience laughing)

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.810
Now, even after Willa was
diagnosed with cancer,

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:22.360
she continues to provide hot meals

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:25.570
for those kids even while
going through chemo.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:27.284
- Oh my gosh, so selfless.

00:01:27.284 --> 00:01:29.846
(audience applauding)

00:01:29.846 --> 00:01:31.670
Well, we have Willa on the line y'all,

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:34.210
but she thinks that it's just to tell us

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:36.420
about her efforts to help
kids, which is beautiful,

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:37.850
and we would have her here
in the first place for that,

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:41.053
but she has no idea, she's
today's real-life Santa.

00:01:41.053 --> 00:01:42.397
(upbeat music)

00:01:42.397 --> 00:01:45.989
♪ Real-life Santa ♪

00:01:45.989 --> 00:01:48.020
(audience applauding)

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:49.270
All right, let's bring Willa up,

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:51.370
but don't spoil the
surprise, she doesn't know.

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:52.530
Okay, Grinch?

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:54.980
Okay.
(audience laughing)

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:58.082
Hi Willa, I'm Kelly
Clarkson, nice to meet you!

00:01:58.082 --> 00:02:01.249
(audience applauding)

00:02:03.598 --> 00:02:05.830
- I'm so glad to see you.

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:08.220
- I am so honored to meet you,

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:09.660
I've heard so many wonderful things

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:12.100
about you and your heart,
and you are just so selfless.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.640
So we're so inspired by
what you do for kids.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.190
How did this all start?

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:18.610
- I used to work for the state of Texas

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:21.001
and I landed in Athens.

00:02:21.001 --> 00:02:24.630
And once I wanted to just
do hot meals for the kids,

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.650
because I know what it
felt like to grow up,

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:30.560
to struggle and be served nasty food

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.220
at different centers and stuff like that.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:35.447
And I said, "When I grow up,
I'm gonna serve kids hot food

00:02:35.447 --> 00:02:37.330
"if I ever got the opportunity."

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:39.380
And that's what I have been doing,

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:42.990
serving kids hot meals, home cooked meals.

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:44.890
I'm not known as Willa in Athens,

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:47.010
I'm known as the food lady.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:48.700
And I am so glad
(audience laughing)

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.980
to be a part of that community.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:52.500
Since the pandemic has hit,

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.730
it has really hurt my funding so bad

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.737
because when school was let out

00:02:57.737 --> 00:02:59.780
and the kids couldn't go to school,

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.907
of course, the people started calling

00:03:01.907 --> 00:03:04.090
"Ms. Willa, how can you help us

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:05.400
feed our children and stuff?"

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:06.550
So I said, "Okay."

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:08.560
So that's what happened to our funding.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:11.820
But every year I try to do something big

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.310
for my kids in Athens, Texas,

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:16.640
for us during the Christmas holiday time.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:19.029
One year I did a bicycle parade,

00:03:19.029 --> 00:03:19.862
this year--
- Oh my gosh!

00:03:19.862 --> 00:03:22.270
- I wanna do a whole nother
different kind parade

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:24.650
just giving out toys and hot meals.

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:27.110
- Oh my God, and a little
bit goes a long way, right?

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:28.537
When it comes to helping, right?

00:03:28.537 --> 00:03:31.593
- But I like to do big
things 'cause I'm from Texas.

00:03:31.593 --> 00:03:34.501
(audience laughing)

00:03:34.501 --> 00:03:35.992
we do big things, baby.

00:03:35.992 --> 00:03:39.647
(audience applauding)

00:03:39.647 --> 00:03:40.840
- I didn't mean what you were doing,

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:43.540
I meant everybody helping
out in their little ways,

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:44.680
actually goes along way.

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:46.790
I know you go big, I
saw the belt, the shirt.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:49.060
We are the same, we come
from the same place.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:51.910
So I love it, I go
bigger, go home as well.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:53.420
But we happen to have someone here

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.440
who says that you're the real-live Santa.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.190
So I think you know this other Kelli.

00:03:58.190 --> 00:03:59.771
Do you know this Kelli right here?

00:03:59.771 --> 00:04:02.870
(audience applauding)

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:03.857
- Hi Ms. Willa!

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:07.240
- You wanted to say something, right?

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:11.420
- [Kelli] Yes, and we're
both gonna cry, Willa.

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:12.910
- Oh God, now I'm going to, oh no.

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:14.230
- I know, we need tissues.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:16.850
- My makeup artist is
gonna hate me, oh God.

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:19.860
- Willa, I have done lots of stories

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.680
through my journalism career,

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:23.483
but you've touched my heart.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:29.340
You truly help kids, and
you are our real-life Santa.

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:32.737
I love you, you have a heart of gold.

00:04:32.737 --> 00:04:34.330
(audience applauding)

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.490
- Oh my gosh, you two.

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:38.600
Well, Willa, you are a real-life Santa.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:40.610
And we mean in a big way, not a small way,

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:41.770
remember, I said that.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:43.830
And that's just not in
the name as well though,

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:46.900
Pilot G-2 Gel ink pen is
designed for overachievers,

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:49.080
just like you ma'am, with big hearts.

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:50.630
And that's why Pilot's using their pen

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:53.279
to write you a check for
$5,000, will that help?

00:04:53.279 --> 00:04:55.124
(audience applauding)

00:04:55.124 --> 00:04:57.541
- Yes, it'll help, thank you.

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:03.160
- Oh my gosh, and I just wanted to add,

00:05:04.383 --> 00:05:05.750
since you're from my home state

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.060
and I was also one of those kids

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:08.737
that grew up on that
kind of food, nasty food,

00:05:08.737 --> 00:05:10.520
and I was like, "I will help when I can."

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:13.323
I'm gonna double it, and I'm
gonna give you five more.

00:05:13.323 --> 00:05:15.857
- Oh my God.
So that's 10 grand total!

00:05:15.857 --> 00:05:17.798
Thank you so much, Willa.

00:05:17.798 --> 00:05:18.631
(audience applauding)

00:05:18.631 --> 00:05:21.024
We love you, we appreciate
you, we're lifting you up,

00:05:21.024 --> 00:05:22.474
and we're thinking about you.

